    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's what I implemented for the salutation feature.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `POST /api/owners` to accept an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `salutation = title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. Since the value must survive the POST\u2192GET round-trip (GET reloads from the DB, and the test DB uses `ddl-auto=none` with an explicit `schema.sql`), `title` has to be persisted.\n\nChanges (kept to the minimum set, each edit small and low-complexity):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (request field) to `OwnerFields` and a read-only `salutation` (response field) to `Owner`. Both plain strings, so the generated DTOs map directly with no enum conversion.\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column plus its getter/setter (title is Owner-specific; putting it on the shared `Person` superclass would have leaked a column into the `vets` table).\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` deriving `salutation` inline (matching the existing inline `displayName`/`locality` style), avoiding an extra helper file. MapStruct auto-maps `title` in and out by name.\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts (only the hsqldb schema is kept current in this repo; the h2/postgres/mysql schemas already lag behind and aren't used by tests).\n\n`BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner`/`RespondWithOwner` needed no changes \u2014 MapStruct's existing `toOwner`/`toOwnerDto` calls carry `title` through automatically.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** I avoided touching any large or complex function. The only edits to bigger classes were two trivial CC-1 accessors on `Owner`; the mapper change is a single annotation; `BuildOwner` and the response pipeline were left untouched. I also inlined the salutation expression rather than adding a helper class, trading a tiny bit of mapper-expression complexity to avoid multiplying the whole cost by an extra file.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS** (the acceptance suite is the only test module).",
